2. Step forward with one leg, flexing the genous to drop your hanches. Descend until your rear genou nearly touches the ground. Your posture should remain upright, and your front genou should stay above the front foot.
3. Drive through the heel of your lead foot and extend both genous to raise yourself back up.
4. Step forward with your rear foot, Répétezing the lunge on the opposite leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bodyweight_Walking_Lunge/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bosu Ball Cable Crunch With Side Bends', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Connect a standard handle to each arm of a cable machine, and position them in the most downward position.
2. Grab a Bosu Ball and position it in front and center of the cable machine.
3. Lie down on the Bosu Ball with the small of votre dos arched around the ball. Your rear end should be close to le sol without touching it.
4. With both hands, reach back and grab the handle of each cable.
5. With vos pieds positioned in a wide stance, extend vos bras straight out in front of you and in between your genous. vos mains should be at genou level.
6. Keep vos bras straight and in-line with the upward angle of the cable. Elevate your torse in a crunching motion without dropping or bending vos bras.
7. Maintain the rigid position with vos bras. Lentement, descend back to the position de départ with votre dos arched around the Bosu Ball and your abdominals elongated.
8. Répétez the same series of movements to failure.
9. Once you reach failure, keep your abdominaux tight and raise your torse into plank position so votre dos is elevated off the Bosu Ball.
10. Lower vos bras down to your side; keep them straight. Start doing alternating side bends; reach for your heels! This finishing movement will focus on your obliques.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bosu_Ball_Cable_Crunch_With_Side_Bends/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bottoms-Up Clean From The Hang Position', 'Avant-bras', 'Kettlebell', '1. Initiate the exercise by standing upright with a kettlebell in one hand.
2. Swing the kettlebell back forcefully and then reverse the motion forcefully. Crush the kettlebell handle as hard as possible and raise the kettlebell to your épaule.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bottoms-Up_Clean_From_The_Hang_Position/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bottoms Up', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin by lying on votre dos on the ground. vos jambes should be straight and vos bras at your side. C''est votre position de départ.
2. To perform le mouvement, tuck the genous toward your poitrine by flexing the hanches and genous. Following this, extend vos jambes directly above you so that they are perpendiculaire à the ground. Rotate and elevate your pelvis to raise your fessiers from le sol.
3. Après une pause, Revenez en position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bottoms_Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Box Jump (Multiple Response)', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Assume a relaxed stance facing the box or platform approximately an arm''s length away. Arms should be down at the sides and legs slightly bent.
2. Using the arms to aid in the initial burst, jump upward and forward, landing with feet simultaneously on top of the box or platform.
3. Immediately drop or jump back down to the original starting place; then Répétez the sequence.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Box_Jump_Multiple_Response/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Box Skip', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. You will need several boxes lined up about 8 feet apart.
2. Begin facing the first box with one leg slightly behind the other.
3. Drive off the back leg, attempting to gain as much height with the hanches as possible.
4. Immediately upon landing on the box, drive the other leg forward and upward to gain height and distance, leaping from the box. Land between the first two boxes with the same leg that landed on the first box.
5. Then, step to the next box and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Box_Skip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Box Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. The box squat allows you to squat to desired depth and develop explosive strength in the squat movement. Begin in a power rack with a box at the appropriate height behind you. Typically, you would aim for a box height that brings you to a parallel squat, but you can train higher or lower if desired.
2. Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the épaules. Squeeze your omoplates together and rotate your coudes forward, attempting to bend the bar across your épaules. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place vos pieds wider for more emphasis on the back, fessiers, adductors, and ischio-jambiers, or closer together for more quad development. Keep votre tête facing forward.
3. With votre dos, épaules, and sangle abdominale tight, push your genous and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hanches until you are seated on the box. Ideally, your shins should be perpendiculaire à the ground. Pause when you reach the box, and relax the hanche flexors. Never bounce off of a box.
4. Keeping the poids on your heels and pushing vos pieds and genous out, drive upward off of the box as you lead le mouvement with votre tête. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Box_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Box Squat with Bands', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin in a power rack with a box at the appropriate height behind you. Set up the bands on the sleeves, secured to either band pegs, the rack, or haltères so that there is appropriate tension. If haltères are used, secure them so that they don''t move. Also, ensure that the haltères you are using are heavy enough for the bands that you are using. Additional plates can be used to hold the haltères down. If more tension is needed, you can either widen the base on le sol or choke the bands. Typically, you would aim for a box height that brings you to a parallel squat, but you can train higher or lower if desired.
2. Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the épaules. Squeeze your omoplates together and rotate your coudes forward, attempting to bend the bar across your épaules. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place vos pieds wider for more emphasis on the back, fessiers, adductors, and ischio-jambiers, or closer together for more quad development. Keep votre tête facing forward.
3. With votre dos, épaules, and sangle abdominale tight, push your genous and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hanches until you are seated on the box. Ideally, your shins should be perpendiculaire à the ground. Pause when you reach the box, and relax the hanche flexors. Never bounce off of a box.
4. Keeping the poids on your heels and pushing vos pieds and genous out, drive upward off of the box as you lead le mouvement with votre tête. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe. Use care to return the barre to the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Box_Squat_with_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Box Squat with Chains', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin in a power rack with a box at the appropriate height behind you. Typically, you would aim for a box height that brings you to a parallel squat, but you can train higher or lower if desired.
2. To set up the chains, begin by looping the leader chain over the sleeves of the bar. The heavy chain should be attached using a snap hook. Adjust the length of the lead chain so that a few links are still on le sol at the top of le mouvement.
3. Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the épaules. Squeeze your omoplates together and rotate your coudes forward, attempting to bend the bar across your épaules. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place vos pieds wider for more emphasis on the back, fessiers, adductors, and ischio-jambiers, or closer together for more quad development. Keep votre tête facing forward.
4. With votre dos, épaules, and sangle abdominale tight, push your genous and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hanches until you are seated on the box. Ideally, your shins should be perpendiculaire à the ground. Pause when you reach the box, and relax the hanche flexors. Never bounce off of a box.
5. Keeping the poids on your heels and pushing vos pieds and genous out, drive upward off of the box as you lead le mouvement with votre tête. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Box_Squat_with_Chains/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Brachialis-SMR', 'Biceps', 'Foam roller', '1. Lie on your side, with your upper arm against the foam roller. The upper arm should be more or less aligned with votre corps, with the outside of the biceps pressed against the foam roller.
2. Raise your hanches off of le sol, supporting your poids on your arm and on vos pieds. Maintenez 10-30 secondes, and then switch sides.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Brachialis-SMR/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Bradford/Rocky Presses', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Sit on a Military Press banc with a bar at épaule level with a pronated grip (paumes vers l''avant). Conseil : Your grip should be wider than épaule width and it should create a angle de 90 degrés between the forearm and the upper arm as the barre goes down. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Once you pick up the barre with the correct grip, lift the bar up over votre tête by locking vos bras.
3. Now lower the bar down to the back of the head Lentement, as you inspirez.
4. Lift the bar back up to the position de départ as you expirez.
5. Lower the bar down to the position de départ Lentement, as you inspirez. This is one repetition.
6. Alternate in this manner until you complete the recommended amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Bradford_Rocky_Presses/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Butt-Ups', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin a pushup position but with your coudes on the ground and resting on your forearms. vos bras should be bent at a angle de 90 degrés.
2. Arch votre dos slightly out rather than keeping votre dos completely straight.
3. Raise your fessiers toward the ceiling, squeezing your abdominaux tightly to close the distance between your ribcage and hanches. The end result will be that you''ll end up in a high bridge position. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
4. Lower back down Lentement, to your position de départ as you Inspirez. Conseil : Don''t let votre dos sag downwards.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Butt-Ups/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Butt Lift (Bridge)', 'Fessiers', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on votre dos with the hands by your side and your genous bent. vos pieds should be placed around épaule width. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Pushing mainly with your heels, lift your hanches off le sol while keeping votre dos straight. Expirez as you perform this part of the motion and hold at the top for a second.
3. Lentement, go back to the position de départ as you Inspirez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Butt_Lift_Bridge/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Butterfly', 'Pectoraux', 'Machine', '1. Sit on the machine with votre dos flat on the pad.
2. Take hold of the handles. Conseil : Your upper arms should be positioned parallèle au sol; adjust the machine accordingly. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Push the handles together Lentement, as you squeeze your poitrine in the middle. Expirez during this part of the motion and hold the contraction for a second.
4. Return back to the position de départ Lentement, as you inspirez until your poitrine muscles are fully stretched.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Butterfly/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Chest Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Poulie', '1. Adjust the poids to an appropriate amount and be seated, grasping the handles. Your upper arms should be about 45 degrees to the body, with votre tête and poitrine up. The coudes should be bent to about 90 degrees. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by extending through the coude, pressing the handles together straight in front of you. Keep your omoplates retracted as you execute le mouvement.
3. After pausing at full extension, return to th position de départ, keeping tension on the cables.
4. You can also execute this movement with votre dos off the pad, at an incline or decline, or alternate hands.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Chest_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Crossover', 'Pectoraux', 'Poulie', '1. To get yourself into the position de départ, place the pulleys on a high position (above votre tête), select the resistance to be used and hold the pulleys in each hand.
2. Step forward in front of an imaginary straight line between both pulleys while pulling vos bras together in front of you. Your torse should have a small forward bend from the waist. C''est votre position de départ.
3. With a slight bend on your coudes in order to prevent stress at the biceps tendon, extend vos bras to the side (straight out at both sides) in a wide arc until you feel a stretch on your poitrine. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Keep in mind that throughout le mouvement, the arms and torse should remain stationary; le mouvement should only occur at the épaule joint.
4. Return vos bras back to the position de départ as you Expirez. Make sure to use the same arc of motion used to lower the poids.
5. Maintenez la position 1 seconde at the position de départ and Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Crossover/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Kneel below a high pulley that contains a rope attachment.
2. Grasp cable rope attachment and lower the rope until vos mains are placed next to your face.
3. Flex your hanches slightly and allow the poids to hyperextend the lower back. C''est votre position de départ.
4. With the hanches stationary, flex the waist as you contract the abdominaux so that the coudes travel towards the middle of the cuisses. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement and hold the contraction for a second.
5. Lentement, Revenez en position de départ as you inspirez. Conseil : Make sure that you keep constant tension on the abdominaux throughout le mouvement. Also, do not choose a poids so heavy that the lower back handles the brunt of the work.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Deadlifts', 'Quadriceps', 'Poulie', '1. Move the cables to the bottom of the towers and select an appropriate poids. Stand directly in between the uprights.
2. To begin, squat down be flexing your hanches and genous until you can reach the handles.
3. After grasping them, begin your ascent. Driving through your heels extend your hanches and genous keeping vos mains hanging at your side. Keep votre tête and poitrine up throughout le mouvement.
4. After reaching a full standing position, Revenez en position de départ and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Deadlifts/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Hammer Curls - Rope Attachment', 'Biceps', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a rope attachment to a low pulley and stand facing the machine about 12 inches away from it.
2. Grasp the rope with a neutral (palms-in) grip and stand straight up keeping the natural arch of the back and your torse stationary.
3. Put your coudes in by your side and keep them there stationary during the entire movement. Conseil : Only the forearms should move; not your upper arms. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Using your biceps, pull vos bras up as you expirez until your biceps touch your forearms. Conseil : Remember to keep the coudes in and your upper arms stationary.
5. After a 1 second contraction where you squeeze your biceps, Lentement, start to bring the poids back to the original position.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Hammer_Curls_-_Rope_Attachment/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Hip Adduction', 'Quadriceps', 'Poulie', '1. Stand in front of a low pulley facing forward with one leg next to the pulley and the other one away.
2. Attach the cheville cuff to the cable and also to the cheville of the leg that is next to the pulley.
3. Now step out and away from the stack with a wide stance and grasp the bar of the pulley system.
4. Stand on the foot that does not have the cheville cuff (the far foot) and allow the leg with the cuff to be pulled towards the low pulley. C''est votre position de départ.
5. Now perform le mouvement by moving the leg with the cheville cuff in front of the far leg by using the inner cuisses to abduct the hanche. Expirez during this portion of le mouvement.
6. Lentement, Revenez en position de départ as you Inspirez.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and then Répétez the same movement with the opposite leg.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Hip_Adduction/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Incline Pushdown', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Lie on incline an banc facing away from a high pulley machine that has a straight bar attachment on it.
2. Grasp the straight bar attachment overhead with a pronated (overhand; palms down) épaule width grip and extend vos bras in front of you. The bar should be around 2 inches away from your upper cuisses. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping the upper arms stationary, lift vos bras back in a semi circle until the bar is straight over votre tête. Inspirez during this portion of le mouvement.
4. Lentement, go back to the position de départ using your lats and hold the contraction once you reach the position de départ. Expirez during the execution of this movement.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Incline_Pushdown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Incline Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Lie on incline an banc facing away from a high pulley machine that has a straight bar attachment on it.
2. Grasp the straight bar attachment overhead with a pronated (overhand; palms down) prise serrée (less than épaule width) and keep your coudes tucked in to your sides. Your upper arms should create around a angle de 25 degrés when measured from le sol.
3. Keeping the upper arms stationary, extend the arms as you flex the triceps. Expirez during this portion of le mouvement and hold the contraction for a second.
4. Lentement, go back to the position de départ.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Incline_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Internal Rotation', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Sit next to a low pulley sideways (with legs stretched in front of you or crossed) and grasp the single hand cable attachment with the arm nearest to the cable. Conseil : If you can adjust the pulley''s height, you can use a flat banc to sit on instead.
2. Position the coude against your side with the coude bent at 90° and the arm pointing towards the pulley. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Pull the single hand cable attachment toward votre corps by internally rotating your épaule until your forearm is across your abdominaux. You will be creating an imaginary semi-circle. Conseil : The forearm should be perpendiculaire à your torse en permanence.
4. Lentement, go back to the initial position.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and then Répétez le mouvement with the next arm.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Internal_Rotation/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Iron Cross', 'Pectoraux', 'Poulie', '1. Begin by moving the pulleys to the high position, select the resistance to be used, and take a handle in each hand.
2. Stand directly between both pulleys with vos bras extended out to your sides. votre tête and poitrine should be up while vos bras form a "T". C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping the coudes extended, pull vos bras straight to your sides.
4. Return vos bras back to the position de départ Après une pause, at the peak contraction.
5. Continue le mouvement for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Iron_Cross/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Judo Flip', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Connect a rope attachment to a tower, and move the cable to the lowest pulley position. Tenez-vous debout avec your side to the cable with a wide stance, and grab the rope with both hands.
2. Twist votre corps away from the pulley as you bring the rope over your épaule like you''re performing a judo flip.
3. Shift your poids between vos pieds as you twist and crunch forward, pulling the cable downward.
4. Revenez en position de départ and Répétez until failure.
5. Then, reposition and Répétez the same series of movements on the opposite side.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Judo_Flip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Lying Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat and grasp the straight bar attachment of a low pulley with a narrow prise en pronation. Conseil : The easiest way to do this is to have someone hand you the bar as you lay down.
2. With vos bras extended, position the bar over your torse. vos bras and your torse should create a angle de 90 degrés. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lower the bar by bending at the coude while keeping the upper arms stationary and coudes in. Go down until the bar lightly touches your forehead. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
4. Flex the triceps as you lift the bar back to its position de départ. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
5. Maintenez la position 1 seconde at the contracted position and Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Lying_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable One Arm Tricep Extension', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. With your right hand, grasp a single handle attached to the high-cable pulley using a supinated (underhand; paumes vers up) grip. You should be standing directly in front of the poids stack.
2. Now pull the handle down so that your upper arm and coude are locked in to the side of votre corps. Your upper arm and forearm should form an acute angle (less than 90-degrees). You can keep the other arm by the waist and you can have one leg in front of you and the other one back for better balance. C''est votre position de départ.
3. As you contract the triceps, move the single handle attachment down to your side until your arm is straight. Expirez as you perform this movement. Conseil : Only the forearms should move. Your upper arms should remain stationary en permanence.
4. Squeeze the triceps and Maintenez la position 1 seconde in this contracted position.
5. Lentement, return the handle to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and then perform the same movement with the other arm.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_One_Arm_Tricep_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Preacher Curl', 'Biceps', 'Poulie', '1. Place a preacher banc about 2 feet in front of a pulley machine.
2. Attach a straight bar to the low pulley.
3. Sit at the preacher banc with your coude and upper arms firmly on top of the banc pad and have someone hand you the bar from the low pulley.
4. Grab the bar and fully extend vos bras on top of the preacher banc pad. C''est votre position de départ.
5. Now start pilling the poids up towards your épaules and squeeze the biceps hard at the top of le mouvement. Expirez as you perform this motion. Also, Maintenez la position 1 seconde at the top.
6. Now Lentement, lower the poids to the position de départ.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Preacher_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Rear Delt Fly', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Adjust the pulleys to the appropriate height and adjust the poids. The pulleys should be above votre tête.
2. Grab the left pulley with your right hand and the right pulley with your left hand, crossing them in front of you. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Initiate le mouvement by moving vos bras back and outward, keeping vos bras straight as you execute le mouvement.
4. Pause at the end of the motion before returning the handles to the start position.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Rear_Delt_Fly/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Reverse Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Connect an cheville strap attachment to a low pulley cable and position a mat on le sol in front of it.
2. Sit down with vos pieds toward the pulley and attach the cable to your chevilles.
3. Lie down, elevate vos jambes and bend your genous at a angle de 90 degrés. vos jambes and the cable should be aligned. If not, adjust the pulley up or down until they are.
4. With vos mains behind votre tête, bring your genous inward to your torse and elevate your hanches off le sol.
5. Pause for a moment and in a slow and controlled manner drop your hanches and bring vos jambes back to the starting angle de 90 degrés. You should still have tension on your abdominaux in the resting position.
6. Répétez the same movement to failure.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Reverse_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Rope Overhead Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a rope to the bottom pulley of the pulley machine.
2. Grasping the rope with both hands, extend vos bras with vos mains directly above votre tête using a neutral grip (paumes vers each other). Your coudes should be in close to votre tête and the arms should be perpendiculaire à le sol with the knuckles aimed at the ceiling. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lentement, lower the rope behind votre tête as you hold the upper arms stationary. Inspirez as you perform this movement and pause when your triceps are fully stretched.
4. Revenez en position de départ by flexing your triceps as you Expirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Rope_Overhead_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Rope Rear-Delt Rows', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Sit in the same position on a low pulley row station as you would if you were doing seated cable rows for the back.
2. Attach a rope to the pulley and grasp it with an prise en pronation. vos bras should be extended and parallèle au sol with the coudes flared out.
3. Keep your lower back upright and slide your hanches back so that your genous are slightly bent. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Pull the cable attachment towards your upper poitrine, just below the neck, as you keep your coudes up and out to the sides. Continue this motion as you expirez until the coudes travel slightly behind the back. Conseil : Keep your upper arms horizontal, perpendiculaire à the torse and parallèle au sol throughout the motion.
5. Go back to the initial position where the arms are extended and the épaules are stretched forward. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Rope_Rear-Delt_Rows/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Russian Twists', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Connect a standard handle attachment, and position the cable to a middle pulley position.
2. Lie on a stability ball perpendiculaire à the cable and grab the handle with one hand. You should be approximately arm''s length away from the pulley, with the tension of the poids on the cable.
3. Grab the handle with both hands and fully extend vos bras above your poitrine. You hands should be directly in-line with the pulley. If not, adjust the pulley up or down until they are.
4. Keep your hanches elevated and abdominaux engaged. Rotate your torse away from the pulley for a full-quarter rotation. votre corps should be flat from head to genous.
5. Pause for a moment and in a slow and controlled manner reset to the position de départ. You should still have side tension on the cable in the resting position.
6. Répétez the same movement to failure.
7. Then, reposition and Répétez the same series of movements on the opposite side.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Russian_Twists/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Seated Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Seat on a flat banc with votre dos facing a high pulley.
2. Grasp the cable rope attachment with both hands (with the palms of the hands facing each other) and place vos mains securely over both épaules. Conseil : Allow the poids to hyperextend the lower back slightly. C''est votre position de départ.
3. With the hanches stationary, flex the waist so the coudes travel toward the hanches. Expirez as you perform this step.
4. As you inspirez, go back to the initial position slowly.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Seated_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Seated Lateral Raise', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Stand in the middle of two low pulleys that are opposite to each other and place a flat banc right behind you (in perpendicular fashion to you; the narrow edge of the banc should be the one behind you). Select the poids to be used on each pulley.
2. Now sit at the edge of the flat banc behind you with vos pieds placed in front of your genous.
3. Bend forward while keeping votre dos flat and rest your torse on the cuisses.
4. Have someone give you the single handles attached to the pulleys. Grasp the left pulley with the right hand and the right pulley with the left after you select your poids. The pulleys should run under your genous and vos bras will be extended with paumes vers each other and a slight bend at the coudes. This will be the position de départ.
5. While keeping the arms stationary, raise the upper arms to the sides until they are parallèle au sol and at épaule height. Expirez during the execution of this movement and hold the contraction for a second.
6. Lentement, lower vos bras to the position de départ as you inspirez.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. Conseil : Maintain upper arms perpendiculaire à torse and a fixed coude position (10 degree to angle de 30 degrés) throughout exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Milieu du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Seated_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Shoulder Press', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Move the cables to the bottom of the towers and select an appropriate poids.
2. Stand directly in between the uprights. Grasp the cables and hold them at épaule height, paumes vers l''avant. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping votre tête and poitrine up, extend through the coude to press the handles directly over head.
4. After pausing at the top, Revenez en position de départ and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Shrugs', 'Trapèzes', 'Poulie', '1. Grasp a cable bar attachment that is attached to a low pulley with a épaule width or slightly wider overhand (paumes vers down) grip.
2. Stand erect close to the pulley with vos bras extended in front of you holding the bar. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lift the bar by elevating the épaules as high as possible as you expirez. Hold the contraction at the top for a second. Conseil : The arms should remain extended en permanence. Refrain from using the biceps to help lift the bar. Only the épaules should be moving up and down.
4. Lower the bar back to the original position.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Shrugs/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cable Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Poulie', '1. Start out by placing a flat banc in front of a low pulley cable that has a straight bar attachment.
2. Use vos bras to grab the cable bar with a narrow to épaule width supinated grip (palms up) and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against the top of your cuisses. Your poignets should be hanging just beyond your genous.
3. Start out by curling your poignet upwards and exhaling. Keep the contraction for a second.
4. Lentement, lower your poignets back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
5. Your forearms should be stationary as your poignet is the only movement needed to perform cet exercice.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cable_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Calf-Machine Shoulder Shrug', 'Trapèzes', 'Machine', '1. Position yourself on the calf machine so that the épaule pads are above your épaules. Your torse should be straight with the arms extended normally by your side. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Raise your épaules up towards your ears as you expirez and hold the contraction for a full second.
3. Lentement, Revenez en position de départ as you inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Calf-Machine_Shoulder_Shrug/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Calf Press', 'Mollets', 'Machine', '1. Adjust the seat so that vos jambes are only slightly bent in the start position. The balls of vos pieds should be firmly on the platform.
2. Select an appropriate poids, and grasp the handles. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Straighten the legs by extending the genous, just barely lifting the poids from the stack. Your cheville should be fully flexed, toes pointing up. Execute le mouvement by pressing downward through the balls of vos pieds as far as possible.
4. Après une pause, reverse the motion and Répétez.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Calf_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Calf Press On The Leg Press Machine', 'Mollets', 'Machine', '1. Using a leg press machine, sit down on the machine and place vos jambes on the platform directly in front of you at a medium (épaule width) foot stance.
2. Lower the safety bars holding the weighted platform in place and press the platform all the way up until vos jambes are fully extended in front of you without locking your genous. (Note: In some leg press units you can leave the safety bars on for increased safety. If your leg press unit allows for this, then this is the preferred method of performing the exercise.) Your torse and the legs should make perfect angle de 90 degrés. Now carefully place your toes and balls of vos pieds on the lower portion of the platform with the heels extending off. Toes should be facing forward, outwards or inwards as described at the beginning of the chapter. C''est votre position de départ.
